course: dictionary
lesson: 4806
title: Humorous words and jokes
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A humorous piece of writing makes you laugh or smile. Writers choose their words carefully to make you feel that way. «Not the sharpest knife in the drawer» sounds like it is about cutlery, but it is a joke: it means someone is not very clever.
explain: Humorous can describe a story, a poem or a person. A humorous person likes to joke. A writer may write in a humorous way, so the reader smiles even when the events are silly. Look for clues such as a surprising word, a silly picture in your mind, or an odd comparison.
explain: Some humorous phrases are used only in certain countries. «Popped his clogs» is British English for died, but it is said as a joke, not to be sad. «Not our finest hour» is a funny way of admitting a bad failure. When a phrase seems silly, ask yourself: is the writer making a joke?
fact: Humorous means funny, or showing a sense of humour.
fact: Humorous is an adjective: a humorous story, a humorous person.
fact: Humorously is the adverb: he spoke humorously about his mistake.
fact: Before -ous, the u in humour is usually dropped: humour becomes humorous.
fact: Glamour follows the same pattern: glamour becomes glamorous.
fact: «Unmentionables» is a humorous word for underwear.
exercise: Which word means funny? | Hungry | *Humorous | Humble | Hidden
exercise: «Not the sharpest knife in the drawer» is a humorous phrase. What does it mean? | Someone who cuts things well | *Not very clever | A dull kitchen tool | A knife that is hard to find
exercise: Which word is the adverb from humorous? | Humorous | *Humorously | Humour | Humours
test: Which is the correct spelling of the adjective from humour? | Humourous | Humorus | *Humorous | Humorouse
test: The teacher read «a humorous poem» to the class. What does humorous mean here? | Lost and confused | *Funny, making people smile | Loud and angry | Sad and quiet
exam: «Popped his clogs» is humorous British English. What does it mean? | Went to bed early | Lost his shoes | *Died, said as a joke | Ran very fast
